{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"chapter-notes","type":"text","text":"# notes/theology/\n\n149 chapter notes\n17 scholars covered\n\nFormat per chapter:\n## Claim N\n→ Evidence type\n→ Confidence rating\n→ Stakes assessment\n→ Scholarly disagreement\n→ Cross-references\n\n[[Notes Index]]","x":-680,"y":380,"width":290,"height":420,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"sources","type":"text","text":"# Sources\n\n## Books (17)\nSmith, Romer, Day, Dever, Cross,\nLewis, Sommer, Heiser, Kaufmann,\nTigay, Schmid, Keel & Uehlinger,\nAlbertz, Stavrakopoulou, Fleming,\nZevit, Friedman\n\n## Primary Sources (11)\n- Soleb Shasu inscription\n- Kuntillet Ajrud inscriptions\n- Khirbet el-Qom inscription\n- Deut 32:8-9 (DSS/LXX/MT)\n- Merneptah Stele\n- Elephantine Papyri\n- Ugaritic Baal Cycle\n- Mesha Stele\n- Tel Dan Stele\n- Lachish Ostraca\n- Ketef Hinnom amulets\n\n[[Sources Index]]","x":-680,"y":-600,"width":290,"height":670,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"pipeline","type":"text","text":"# OSKG-YahWeh Pipeline\n\n## Phase 0: Source Ingestion\n17 scholarly books\nMonographs read chapter-by-chapter\n\n## Phase 1: Chapter Notes\n149 structured notes, ~466KB\n`obsidian-book-notes` skill\nClaim → Evidence → Confidence → Stakes\n\n## Phase 2: Claims Extraction\n723 discrete claim nodes\nYAML frontmatter + typed edges\nLLM + human-in-the-loop\n\n## Phase 3: Graph Construction\nTyped edges (intra-scholar + cross-scholar)\nSupports · Contradicts · Depends on · Challenged by\n\n## Phase 4: Structural Analysis\n4 synthesis phases:\n1. Hinge inventory (load-bearing claims)\n2. Cascade trees (collapse radii)\n3. Counter-position stress tests\n4. Unknowns & convergence detection\n\n## Phase 5: Capstone Synthesis\nEvidence-density map\nSettled convergences + genuine unknowns\nGraph fragility analysis\n\n---\n**See:** [[METHODOLOGY]]\n**Claims:** [[notes/claims-architecture]]","x":130,"y":-760,"width":350,"height":1180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"orkg","type":"text","text":"# ORKG\nOpen Research Knowledge Graph\n\n**(Auer, D'Souza, Farfar et al.)**\nLeibniz University Hannover\nSince ~2019\n\n## Reference Implementation\n\nThe canonical OSKG: millions of papers,\nstructured claim extraction, typed\nsemantic edges, SPARQL querying,\nevidence synthesis from graph structure.\n\n## Same Architecture\n\n**Ingestion:** LLM + human-in-loop\n**Structuring:** Semantic claim nodes\n**Enrichment:** Typed cross-paper edges\n**Synthesis:** Graph-driven evidence synthesis\n\n## Key References\n\nAuer et al. (2025) — flagship, 20+ citations\nTan & D'Souza (2026) — LLM extraction for meta-analysis\nAggarwal (2026) — human-in-loop extraction model\nSander (2025) — LLM reasoning over ORKG graphs\n\n## OSKG-YahWeh vs ORKG\n\nORKG: scale (millions of papers, broad coverage)\nOSKG-YahWeh: depth (723 claims, chapter-level\nfidelity, humanities domain)\n\nComplementary: the same architecture validated\nat both ends of the scale-depth spectrum.\n\n---\n**Full analysis:** [[METHODOLOGY]]","x":850,"y":-760,"width":360,"height":1210,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"claims","type":"text","text":"# notes/claims/\n\n723 claim nodes\n\n**Edge types:**\n- supports\n- contradicts\n- depends on\n- challenged by\n\n**Filterable by:**\nTopic · Scholar · Evidence type\nConfidence · Claim type\n\n**Quality:** Every claim traced\nto a specific passage in a\nspecific chapter.\n\n[[notes/claims-architecture]]","x":-390,"y":880,"width":290,"height":480,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"synthesis","type":"text","text":"# Synthesis Phases\n\n## Phase 1: Hinge Inventory\nTop 25 load-bearing claims\nHinge #3: 65 dependents (Yahweh-El distinct)\n\n## Phase 2: Cascade Trees\nBFS to 4 levels deep\nCollapse radius for top 5 hinges\n\n## Phase 3: Stress Tests\nSurvival rates:\nHeiser 72% · Schmid 41%\nTigay 85% · Kaufmann 58%\n\n## Phase 4: Convergence & Unknowns\n8 settled convergences\n4 genuine unknowns\n\n[[notes/synthesis/phase1-hinge-inventory]]\n[[notes/synthesis/phase2-cascade-trees]]\n[[notes/synthesis/phase3-counter-position-stress-tests]]\n[[notes/synthesis/phase4-unknowns-and-convergence]]","x":280,"y":640,"width":350,"height":800,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"capstone","type":"text","text":"# Capstone\n\n**What the graph shows**\n\n## Settled (8 convergences)\nEl as original god (16 supports)\nYahweh southern origin (6+ scholars)\nTwo-religion model (10 supports)\nArchaeology primary for folk religion\nMonotheism as transformed myth\nJerusalem centralization late political project\nBes figures not Yahweh & Asherah\nEl family/clan deity vs national Yahweh\n\n## Contested (4 fault lines)\nAsherah: goddess vs symbol\nThe central unresolved question\nDeut 32:8-9: two gods or one\nMonotheism: early revolution or late evolution\nIsraelite uniqueness vs ANE normality\n\n## Fragilities\nChronological assumption (Schmid: 41% survival)\nKaufmann instability (most cited + most contradicted)\nAsherah impasse (different epistemological standards)\nSupport asymmetry (dissenters structurally disadvantaged)\n\n[[notes/synthesis/capstone-what-does-this-mean]]","x":30,"y":1640,"width":550,"height":840,"color":"4"}
	],
